{"name":"Ship Shape","hex":"#709797","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ship-shape","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Archaic spelling of shipshape."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Archaic spelling of shipshape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ship-shape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ship","blocks":[{"text":"A ship is a large watercraft designed for travel across the surface of a body of water, carrying cargo or passengers, or in support of specialized tasks such as warfare, oceanography and fishing. Ships are generally distinguished from boats, based on size, shape, load capacity and purpose. Ships have supported exploration, trade, warfare, migration, colonization, and science. Ship transport is responsible for the largest portion of world commerce."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolten.4.phb.ajb.jpg/330px-Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolten.4.phb.ajb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship","wikidata":"Q11446"},{"title":"Shape","blocks":[{"text":"A shape is a graphical representation of an object's form or its external boundary, outline, or external surface. It is distinct from other object properties, such as color, texture, or material type.\nIn geometry, shape excludes information about the object's position, size, orientation and chirality.\nA figure is a representation including both shape and size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Plastic_vormenstoof_of_puzzelbal_van_%E2%80%9CTupperware_Toy%E2%80%9D%2C_objectnr_83212.JPG/330px-Plastic_vormenstoof_of_puzzelbal_van_%E2%80%9CTupperware_Toy%E2%80%9D%2C_objectnr_83212.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shape","wikidata":"Q207961"}],"images":[{"src